GNU Wget for OpenVMS
====================

This is GNU Wget @VERSION@ built natively for OpenVMS @ARCH@, from the
unmodified GNU release plus the patches in the vms-wget project:

    https://github.com/issinoho/vms-wget

Kit version: @KITVERSION@.  Wget is free software under the GNU General
Public License, version 3 or later; see COPYING.  The manual is WGET.TXT;
the startup-file commands are described in SAMPLE.WGETRC.

What is installed
-----------------
    WGET$ROOT:[BIN]WGET.EXE          wget
    WGET$ROOT:[ETC]WGETRC.           the system-wide startup file
    WGET$ROOT:[SSL]CACERT.PEM        CA certificates for HTTPS
    WGET$ROOT:[000000]WGET$SETUP.COM defines the wget command
    WGET$ROOT:[DOC]                  this file, COPYING, NEWS, WGET.TXT,
                                     SAMPLE.WGETRC
    SYS$STARTUP:WGET$STARTUP.COM     defines WGET$ROOT

TLS uses VSI's OpenSSL 3.0 kit (SSL3), a prerequisite of this kit; zlib
(--compression=gzip) and PCRE2 (--regex-type=pcre) are linked in.  This
build has no IDN (internationalised domain names), public-suffix list,
metalink or --use-askpass support.

Setting up
----------
The kit installs WGET$STARTUP.COM into SYS$STARTUP and runs it once.  To
define WGET$ROOT at every boot, the system manager adds this line to
SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:

    $ @SYS$STARTUP:WGET$STARTUP.COM

Each user (or SYLOGIN.COM, for everyone) then defines the command:

    $ @WGET$ROOT:[000000]WGET$SETUP.COM

Startup files and CA certificates
---------------------------------
wget reads WGET$ROOT:[ETC]WGETRC. first, then the user's own file:
SYS$LOGIN:.WGETRC, or the file the logical name WGETRC names.  The system
file sets

    ca_certificate = WGET$ROOT:[SSL]CACERT.PEM

so HTTPS servers are verified against Mozilla's root certificates as
extracted by the curl project (https://curl.se/docs/caextract.html), dated
@CABUNDLEDATE@.  The kit replaces WGETRC. on upgrade; to keep site settings,
put them in a file of your own and define the logical name SYSTEM_WGETRC
to point at it.  --ca-certificate=file overrides the bundle for one run.

Upper-case options and batch jobs
---------------------------------
Under the TRADITIONAL DCL parse style DCL upper-cases the unquoted parts of
a command and the C run-time library passes them to wget in lower case, so
an unquoted -O arrives as -o (log file) and -N as -n.  Batch jobs use
TRADITIONAL even when interactive logins are set to EXTENDED.  Quote the
options that use capital letters, or start the procedure with

    $ SET PROCESS/PARSE_STYLE=EXTENDED

Exit status
-----------
Under DCL a failed run exits with an error-severity status, so ON ERROR and
IF .NOT. $STATUS work; wget's exit code N (4 network failure, 5 certificate
not verified, 8 server error response, ...) is ($STATUS .AND. %X7F8) / 8.
Under a GNV shell, $? is the exit code as on Unix.

Files
-----
Downloads are written as Stream_LF files.  An existing file is not
overwritten or renamed file.1: wget writes a new version of it.  On ODS-2
disks, names from URLs are changed to valid ODS-2 names; on ODS-5 they are
kept.
